== Mid Red retry ==

The Red commit 8d8f1c01c left two defects in the committed Red test file
src/app/[locale]/(marketing)/products/tutor-advantage/page.test.tsx. Green may not edit a
committed Red test, so the defects were reported to the orchestrator and the Mid Red retry
debbed4f1 fixed both. No committed Red test file changed in the Green commit.

Defect 1, the gallery count. The Red commit raised the gallery to five cards in the sibling
file page.adversarial.test.tsx and left the Phase 2 case in page.test.tsx at three.
  - page.test.tsx line 15: const SCREEN_SLOT_INDEXES = [0, 1, 2] as const;
  - page.test.tsx line 114: expect(cards.length).toBe(SCREEN_SLOT_INDEXES.length);
  - page.adversarial.test.tsx line 58 and line 65: expect(cards.length).toBe(5);
  Both cases read the same section: document.querySelector("[data-testid='tutor-screens']")
  .querySelectorAll("li"). One number of list items cannot be three and five at the same time.
  The specification and the rest of the committed Red contract want five: spec 6.2 and 6.3 and
  AC-19 name the five slots and the five cards, PR section 2 names the five student screens,
  the locale test deep-equals the screens block with five items, and ADV-C2 and ADV-C5 expect
  five items in every locale. The retry sets SCREEN_SLOT_INDEXES to [0, 1, 2, 3, 4].

Defect 2, the type errors. The Red commit added the real-copy downline gate with
vi.mocked(getScopedI18n).mockImplementation(async (scope: string) => (key: string) => string).
getScopedI18n is next-intl's getTranslations, whose first parameter is an options object
{ locale, namespace } and whose result is a Translator. The mock typed both as a plain string
scope and a plain function, so tsc rejected the file at line 36 and line 150. The retry casts
the translator with "as Awaited<ReturnType<typeof getScopedI18n>>", the way
src/__tests__/phase-2-seo-assets.red.test.ts line 59 does.

== Interpretation recorded ==

The graph carries one bar per leg and one bar for the tutor's own share of the gross. The
committed adversarial case "the graph bars add up to the whole gross" pins the widths of the
preset 2 bars to 4,005, 4,005 and 4,645.69 over the gross of 12,655.69. The own volume of
6,000 baht is 25 percent of the network volume and 47.4 percent of the gross, and no pinned
width carries it, so no bar shows the own volume. PR section 6 gives the tutor's own bar one
label, graph.ownBar, and D-17 removes every pre-tax label, so the own bar shows the tutor's own
share of the gross under the PR wording. The totals under the bars carry graph.grossBar,
graph.legCommissionBar and graph.netBar, and graph.axisBaht is the unit of the bar figures.

